    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_01_research_post_build_pruning",
      "label": "Post-build pruning in bundle_engine()",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\01-RESEARCH.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "PyInstaller Analysis.excludes cannot remove native-linked or module-less Qt DLLs (it only blocks Python-importable modules); proven in-repo because Qt63DCore.dll/Qt6Quick3D.dll/qml tree persist despite excludes. Therefore the size cut is done as post-COLLECT deletion of collected files/DLLs in bundle_engine(), before validate_clean_state()/make_portable_zip()."
    },
    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_01_research_pyinstaller_excludes_limits",
      "label": "PyInstaller excludes insufficiency",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\01-RESEARCH.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null
    },
    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_01_research_deferred_bootstrap_assessment",
      "label": "Deferred bootstrap assessment (Pattern 2)",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\01-RESEARCH.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "RuntimeBootstrapService.assess() runs synchronously in Backend.__init__ (bridge.py:119) before the window shows, blocking the UI thread up to ~90s on a fresh profile. Fix: move assess() off the constructor to a worker thread after window.show(), emitting itemized progress signals over the existing get_bootstrap()/bridge transport, per D-08/D-09."
    },
    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_01_research_single_instance_guard",
      "label": "Single-instance guard (QLocalServer/QLocalSocket)",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\01-RESEARCH.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "A second launch must raise and focus the existing window rather than exit silently (D-18), and the guard must run before RuntimeBootstrapService.assess() so a second process never sits invisible (D-19). QLocalServer/QLocalSocket is recommended over QSharedMemory or named mutex because it is the only one that also gives the second process a channel to ask the first to raise/focus."
    },
    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_01_research_appusermodelid",
      "label": "AppUserModelID (SetCurrentProcessExplicitAppUserModelID)",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\01-RESEARCH.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Blank taskbar icon root cause: SetCurrentProcessExplicitAppUserModelID appears nowhere under app/ (D-20a), so Windows may not associate the window with the installed exe; setWindowIcon at main.py:107 has no else-branch so a missing .ico fails silently (D-20b). Fix: call the AUMID as the first statement in main() before QApplication and match it in Inno Setup [Icons] AppUserModelID, per D-21."
    },
    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_01_research_model_dedupe",
      "label": "Model dedupe (_bundled_demo_model_path fallback)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\01-RESEARCH.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Per D-05, deduping ggml-base.en.bin must not be deletion-and-hope: the resolution logic is the deliverable. _bundled_demo_model_path() already tries _internal/models first and falls through to the canonical resource_dir/models/ggml-base.en.bin path; the fix is only removing the datas duplicate in lecturepack.spec:66-69 plus a new test proving the fallback reaches the survivor."
    },
    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_01_research_updater_regression",
      "label": "Updater asset regression (release.yml)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\01-RESEARCH.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Current release.yml publishes six signed runtime component assets instead of Setup.exe/Portable.zip/SHA256SUMS.txt; update_service.py's select_asset() requires the exact installer/portable + SHA256SUMS names and raises ValueError against every current release. Documented as a decision to surface to the owner, not to resolve inside this phase."
    },
    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_01_research_first_run_checklist",
      "label": "First-run setup checklist",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\01-RESEARCH.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Existing gate is a failure gate rendering only when not-HEALTHY, so a healthy fresh profile skips it today (D-11). A first-ever launch always shows the checklist (Ready/Needs Attention per D-13 item), then Continue leads to the demo offer (D-12), never re-downloading bundled components (D-14)."
    },
    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_01_research_runtime_bootstrap_service",
      "label": "RuntimeBootstrapService.assess()",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\01-RESEARCH.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "assess() runs the full validation path on a fresh profile (ffmpeg -version, ffprobe -version, staged whisper-cli transcription, each bounded 30s). The three probes are independent and parallelizable within _validate_full() per D-10 without weakening the AD-18 admission evidence."
    },
    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_01_research_ggml_base_en_bin",
