    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_01_ui_spec_checking_state",
      "label": "checking progress state",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\01-UI-SPEC.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "New client state layered on RuntimeSetupGateModel: honest itemized per-component progress shown while assess() runs full validation behind an already-visible window (D-08/D-09). Exactly 5 rows in canonical backend order, one aggregate .lp-fill bar, one aria-live=polite line naming the active check, only Exit action. Renders only on the full path (_requires_full() true), never on warm/light launches."
    },
    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_01_ui_spec_checklist_state",
      "label": "checklist first-run state",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\01-UI-SPEC.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Ready/Needs Attention first-run checklist shown once before the demo offer on any launch where setup is not yet acknowledged (D-12/D-13). Same 5 rows resolved to Ready or Needs Attention; Continue primary + Skip secondary (both byte-identical in effect, per Open Question 3); no Exit (owner-resolved Open Question 1); flag-keyed to setup_acknowledged (D-16), shown once even after repair-then-first-healthy (Open Question 2)."
    },
    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_01_ui_spec_runtime_setup_gate_model",
      "label": "RuntimeSetupGateModel reducer",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\01-UI-SPEC.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Client reducer grows from ['gate','diagnostics','confirm','repairing','offline','failed','ready'] to include checking and checklist. Every existing transition, operation-ID stale-event rule, and terminal-event rule is unchanged; only the entry path into the overlay changes from an invisible bootstrapPending limbo to a visible checking state."
    },
    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_01_ui_spec_anti_flicker_pacing",
      "label": "Anti-flicker pacing rule",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\01-UI-SPEC.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "From BUG-20/21/22's lesson: any rapid backend-driven state flip must be deliberately paced, not accidental. A row must not flip from pending to done in under 100ms; hold each row's checking mark at least --motion-normal (160ms) before showing done, using the existing motion token. Whisper check past ~5s appends 'this can take a few seconds' (text only, no spinner)."
    },
    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_01_ui_spec_ready_vs_mixed_contract",
      "label": "Ready-only vs Mixed visual contract",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\01-UI-SPEC.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "A healthy machine must not see a warning screen. Four of D-13's five items are hard-blocking so are Ready whenever HEALTHY; only 'supported Windows version' is non-blocking and can independently render Needs Attention while HEALTHY. Heading and Continue CTA are identical between Ready-only and Mixed — only the one row's badge differs (yellow .lp-state[data-state=paused] vs green success). The failure gate has different heading/CTA entirely."
    },
    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_01_ui_spec_runtime_setup_overlay",
      "label": "#runtime-setup-overlay",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\01-UI-SPEC.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Both new states render inside the same existing WebEngine overlay scrim/panel (#runtime-setup-overlay, app/ui/index.html:676-693), reusing the inert/focus-trap mechanism (topOverlay(), trapFocus(), setUnderlyingInert()) rather than a parallel one. D-15 ruled out a native Qt pre-window to avoid a second visual language."
    },
    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_01_validation_packaged_gui_verification",
      "label": "Packaged-GUI-launch verification (Wave 0 gap)",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\01-VALIDATION.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "No existing test launches QWebEngineView, so tests/test_runtime_packaged_smoke.py passing does NOT prove WebEngine still renders after the Qt cuts (removing Qt6Quick.dll/Qt6Qml.dll could break WebEngineCore's internal compositor at binary-load level). Highest-value gap: a packaged clean-profile launch must show rendered WebEngine content, not just an icon and non-crashed process."
    },
    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_01_validation_wave_0_gaps",
      "label": "Wave 0 verification gaps",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\01-VALIDATION.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Covered by no existing test: size-measurement of Setup.exe, extended check_clean_state assertions (absent translations/qml/Quick DLLs/Qt6Pdf.dll, one ggml-base.en.bin), packaged-GUI render proof, RuntimeSetupGateModel reducer tests, ConfigManager setup-acknowledged persistence test, two-process single-instance test, and a test proving _bundled_demo_model_path()'s fallback reaches the canonical copy."
    },
    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_01_validation_per_task_verification_map",
      "label": "Per-task verification map",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\01-VALIDATION.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Because no REQUIREMENTS.md IDs map to this phase, ROADMAP Success Criteria act as effective requirement IDs (SC-1..SC-6). Per-task verification map is filled by planner/validate-phase; phase is draft, nyquist_compliant: false until Wave 0 covers all missing references."
    },
    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_deferred_items_send2trash_gap",
      "label": "Send2Trash packaging gap (hard-delete fallback)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\deferred-items.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "app/requirements.txt claims to mirror repo-root requirements.txt but omits Send2Trash, tzdata, yt-dlp, so CI builds (which install -r app/requirements.txt) have never contained them. Send2Trash is a user-data concern: engine_adapter.py:1202's guard 'only a genuinely absent send2trash justifies a hard delete now' means packaged builds permanently delete user files where source intends a recoverable recycle-bin move. Product decision, not a size cut; deferred."
    },
    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_deferred_items_release_trust_stale_fixture",
      "label": "release_trust stale Ed25519 fixture",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\deferred-items.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "tests/fixtures/release_trust/ manifest/signature pair no longer verifies against the production Ed25519 public key rotated at commit 55257a8, causing ReleaseTrustError 'manifest signature verification failed' across test_release_trust.py and downstream (test_settle on release_trust, runtime_packaged_repair, runtime_repair). Also test_release_trust hash-pin assertion wasn't updated after efb99cd/95dd5fb replaced the pinned cryptography wheel with pip install cryptography==49.0.0. Recommends regenerating fixtures against the current key."
    },
    {
      "id": "_planning_phases_01_clean_device_footprint_first_launch_deferred_items_test_package_footprint_stale",
      "label": "test_package_footprint stale 6-target fixture (BUG-27)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\marsh\\Documents\\LecturePack-worktrees\\release-polish\\.planning\\phases\\01-clean-device-footprint-first-launch\\deferred-items.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "tests/test_package_footprint.py still hardcodes 6 cut targets, but BUG-27's fix reduced PRUNABLE_QT_COMPONENTS in build.py to 4 (removed Qt6Qml.dll/Qt6Quick.dll because they are load-bearing link-time dependencies of Qt6WebEngineCore/Qt6WebChannel; pruning them produced a packaged build that could not start). Stale fixture asserts 4==6. Recommend deriving expected count from PRUNABLE_QT_COMPONENTS to prevent future desync."
    }
